CheckMail: request UIDVALIDITY in the STATUS items

Backport of the upstream master fix onto the 0.21.0 release.

handleCheckMailMessage asks the server for MESSAGES/RECENT/UNSEEN/UIDNEXT
and then, for the currently selected mailbox, does `w.selected = status`.
Because UIDVALIDITY was never requested, the replacement MailboxStatus
carries UidValidity == 0, silently discarding the value SELECT returned.
worker/imap/cache.go keys every cached header as

    header.<mailbox>.<w.selected.UidValidity>.<uid>

so from the first CheckMail onward the whole mailbox is written under
`header.<mailbox>.0.<uid>`: the cache namespace no longer changes when the
server invalidates UIDs, which is the exact condition UIDVALIDITY exists to
detect, and entries written before the first CheckMail are orphaned.

Upstream master fixes this by adding imap.StatusUidValidity to the same
items slice. Master additionally surfaces the value on models.DirectoryInfo
via a new `Uid` field (`if status.UidValidity != 0 { info.Uid = ... }`);
that field does not exist in 0.21.0 and is a separate feature, unrelated to
the cache key, so only the items-slice half is backported here.

Zero context (`diff -U0`) on purpose. The insertion point sits inside a
tab-indented Go composite literal, so any context line would begin with the
diff's own leading space followed by a tab -- literal space-before-tab in
this file, which `git diff --check` rejects. A pure-insertion hunk carries
no context lines, so the only added line here starts with `+`, and the hunk
still names the exact line (after checkmail.go:14, `imap.StatusUidNext,`).

Upstream: https://git.sr.ht/~rjarry/aerc/blob/master/worker/imap/checkmail.go

--- a/worker/imap/checkmail.go
+++ b/worker/imap/checkmail.go
@@ -14,0 +15 @@
+		imap.StatusUidValidity,
